  "logline": "First week of classes: a famous atheist demands proof of a soul, a harbor diner needs a dishwasher, and the girl from the porch turns out to be the other half of the assignment.",
  "previously": [
    { "text": "Your father drove you 2,400 miles and saw the Pacific for the first time." },
    { "text": "On the back porch of the Lighthouse, a girl from New Orleans judged a party with you — and then judged you." },
    { "text": "She took the cigarette out of your mouth and kept it.", "if": "e1_lena_took_cig" },
    { "text": "At Mass she wore a mantilla. Afterward you argued about lip service, and you won.", "if": "duel.lipservice.rigor>=3" },
    { "text": "On the stairwell she told someone named Wes she loved him. Then she told him you were nobody.", "if": "e1_stairwell==\"coughed\"" },
    { "text": "Adrian Hale emailed the seminar: come prepared to prove you have a soul. You hit Reply All.", "if": "e1_email_reply==\"replyall\"" }
